{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]There's a cabin in the pines in the [C]hills of [G]Caroline
[G]And a blue eyed girl is waiting there for [D]me
I'm [G]going back some day from her [C]I'll never [G]stray
[G]For she means all the [D]world to [G]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Oh the [C]cabin in the shadow of the [G]pines
[G]And the blue eyed girl way down in [D]Caroline
Some [G]day she'll be my wife we'll [C]live a happy [G]life
In the [G]cabin in the [D]hills of [G]Caroline
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I'm packing my grip for that long long trip
Back to the hills of Caroline
I wanna see that blue eyed girl she's the sweetest in the world
And the cabin in the hills of Caroline
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
And when it's late at night and the moon is shining bright
And the whippoorwill is calling from the hills
Then I'll tell her of my love beneath the stars above
That I love her and I know I always will.
{end_of_chorus}
